      "label": "Thallus Form",
      "description": "Thin, granular or powdery crustose lichen that appears as small, scattered granules rather than a continuous crust",
      "isPrimary": false
    },
    {
      "label": "Size",
      "description": "Very small lichen, typically forming patches less than 5 cm in diameter",
      "isPrimary": false
    }
  ],
  "habitat": "This species thrives in well-lit, dry to moderately moist habitats on calcareous or nutrient-rich substrates such as limestone, concrete, and nutrient-enriched bark throughout New England.",
